{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_88","type":"agent_message","text":"The shared-budget fairness test exposed another issue: if a link’s initial cursor request was deferred, it never retried initialization. That could keep a healthy route stuck after its first visit ran out of budget. Cursor initialization now retries on later ticks, and the healthy route establishes while its sibling is flooded with malformed traffic.\n"}}
